From: Alexander Goodkind <alex@goodkind.io>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mediatek: preserve sibling PPE bindings

Several hardware slots share one software flow bucket. When binding an
unbound slot, __mtk_ppe_check_skb() walks that bucket and clears every
nonmatching flow with a valid hash. This also clears software references
to flows still bound in other slots of the bucket.

With cumulative flow accounting, the next stats request for such a flow
returns its stored previous counters instead of its active hardware
counters. The unsigned delta can then inflate conntrack accounting by
approximately 2^32 bytes and packets. Later requests stop accounting for
traffic still forwarded by the detached hardware flow.

Only clear an old binding when it refers to the hardware slot currently
being replaced. Preserve sibling bindings in the other slots.

Signed-off-by: Alexander Goodkind <alex@goodkind.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
@@ -804,7 +804,7 @@ void __mtk_ppe_check_skb(struct mtk_ppe *ppe, struct sk_buff *skb, u16 hash)
 	hlist_for_each_entry_safe(entry, n, head, list) {
 		if (found ||
 		    !mtk_flow_entry_match(ppe->eth, entry, &foe, entry_len)) {
-			if (entry->hash != 0xffff)
+			if (entry->hash == hash)
 				__mtk_foe_entry_clear(ppe, entry, false);
 			continue;
 		}
